implementationPlan.note:
Created scripts/local-runner/provision.mjs (95 lines).
- **fileImageUrl:** win32 takes only drive-letter paths, with backslashes turned into '/'; POSIX takes absolute paths. No %-encoding; control characters, UNC and device paths give PROVISION_INPUT_INVALID.
- **launchInstance:**
  - validates the owned name, a non-empty string userData and timeoutSeconds in 1..3600;
  - argv is exactly launch <fileUrl> --name n --cloud-init - --timeout T plus launchResourceArgs();
  - it runs through R06 invoker (shell:false, windowsHide, (T+60) s, bounded buffer, SIGKILL);
  - it writes userData to pending.child.stdin, with an error listener for EPIPE, and ends it;
  - a transport without stdin gives PROVISION_LAUNCH_FAILED and the child is SIGKILLed;
  - a rejection gives providerError(classifyFailure).
- **provisionGuest:** input guard, then prerequisites, then:
  - not ready: {provisioned:false, …} with nothing downloaded, reserved or launched;
  - an owned-style primaryName: PRIMARY_NAME_CONFLICT;
  - then buildUserData, ensurePinnedImage, a fileImageUrl precheck, ONE ledger.reserve, R06 provisionOwned (same-name retry) and R07 waitForGuestReady;
  - executionReady is always false, and it never deletes.

Deviations, intended and covered by tests:
- buildUserData runs before the download, so bad bootstrap input never downloads 600 MB.
- The URL uses the host's own path syntax (process.platform), not platform.id; see the step-1 note.
- A precheck refuses an unlaunchable cache path before reserving.

Snapshot full run: 169 tests, 160 pass. The 9 failures are exactly the CLI tests (step 5). W1, W2, W7-W12 and the W14 real-process test pass.
